invariant: INV-26
file: ghash_vector.h
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the host object's reduction multiplies by 0xc400000000000000 where the
  reversed field polynomial needs 0xc200000000000000: its x^7 term moves
  from bit 57 to bit 58, where x^6 sits, so every product with a nonzero
  low half is reduced modulo the wrong polynomial and GHASH answers wrong
  in a host object alone. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof covers
  this code, and bin/ghash_equiv_test is what holds it to gcm.c's
  portable multiply: it compares the multiply, the loop over data and the
  whole AEAD byte for byte. The edit lands in ghash_reduce, which is the
  same C after either instruction, so it compiles on an ARMv8 host and an
  x86-64 one alike and the catch does not depend on which instruction set
  the runner has.

--- old
    ghash_vector constant = ghash_vector_of(GHASH_REDUCTION_WORD, 0);
--- new
    ghash_vector constant = ghash_vector_of(0xc400000000000000U, 0);
